<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Disco started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Disco started.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Lazard Freres said on Tuesday it had started coverage of Argentine retailer Disco SA with a rating of hold.</p>
<p>-- &quot;We believe Disco is a strong competitor in Argentina's retail sector that should produce stable operating performance and real earnings growth for the next few years,&quot; analyst Curtis Butler wrote in a report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;However, the company's stock has appreciated considerably since the IPO (initial public offering) in April and we believe it may be approaching fair value.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's ADR was off 3/8 to 29 in New York on Tuesday.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
